# Which zts internal modules each consumer package may name.
#
# `packages/zts/src/root.zig` re-exports a curated surface (JSValue, Context,
# strip, ...) and, separately, the internal implementation modules. Only the
# internal tier is listed here; the curated surface is ungated.
#
# One row per (package, internal module). Enforced in both directions by
# scripts/check-module-boundary.sh: an unlisted reach fails, and so does a row
# nothing uses. The list only ratchets down - adding a row is a deliberate
# widening of the boundary, and should come with a reason in the commit.
#
# Baseline captured from the tree as it stood when the gate was added; no row
# here is an endorsement, only a record of the reach that already existed.
#
# The four-tier split of packages/zts did not shrink this list, and was not
# expected to once `zts` became a re-export-only umbrella: consumers still
# reach one module, so the compiler enforces direction INSIDE the package
# while this file keeps gating what leaves it. The two checks are
# complementary, not redundant - scripts/check-zts-layering.sh pins tier
# direction, this pins consumer surface.
#
# A row closes when every symbol behind it has a curated name. Measured after
# the split, most rows reach seven to eighteen symbols, and most of what the
# short ones reach is genuinely internal - interpreter.PerfStats,
# string.RopeNode, bytecode_cache.SliceWriter, sqlite.Db. Curating those to
# delete a row would trade a gated internal surface for an ungated public
# one, which is worse. Close a row when the name belongs in the curated
# surface on its own merits, not to make this list shorter.

# runtime
runtime arena
runtime builtins
runtime bytecode
runtime bytes
runtime bytecode_cache
runtime compat
runtime contract_diff
runtime counterexample
runtime equivalence_receipt
runtime file_io
runtime handler_contract
runtime handler_policy
runtime http
# packages/runtime/bench/benchmark.zig reads interpreter.PerfStats to report
# perf counters. Benchmark-only; the counter layout is not stable surface.
runtime interpreter
runtime module_binding
runtime modules
runtime perf_receipt
runtime pipeline
runtime policy
runtime security_events
runtime spec_discharge
runtime string
runtime trace
runtime witness_corpus

